<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_Umbra - the Auroral Umbra                 UtinniPatches
    Authored 2026-09-09 (BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1) as our own copy of the donor AB_PropaneLakes land
    tiles; renamed RUT_FuelSnows 2026-09-21; RENAMED BACK 2026-10-20 on the owner's ruling by card
    (2026-10-19): "it's totally dark except for the utterly beautiful and wildly active aurora. Let's
    call it the Auroral Umbra then. And look back at the original concept sheet to find out about
    precipitation." Then, same day: "Yes, there should be a perpetual Auroral activity in that biome.
    Put that in its def now. Auroral Umbra is the new name, better than Rimefall. And yes, it should
    NOT snow, it should rain propane (equivalent with chemfuel)." Item: AURORAL_UMBRA_RENAME_BACK_TO_DARK.

    Sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_propane_lakes.md (FROZEN; its "not dark, starlit"
    and "it snows fuel" lines are overruled by the two rulings above). The lake is NOT this biome: it
    is RM_TheChill (campaign twin RUT_PropaneLake). The canonical save already carries this defName
    on 2,531 land tiles (census 2026-10-20, tileBiomeDeflate hash 15270), so no repaint is owed for it.
    A save holding the retired name RUT_FuelSnows by NAME resolves here through RUT_UmbraRenameAliases
    (Defs/Misc/RUT_UmbraRename_Aliases.xml); world tiles are saved by shortHash and are not covered,
    but no known save holds the RUT_FuelSnows hash (3528) on any tile.

    MEASURED (sheet SS0, 2026-09-06 export): arc 132-179 (sun 49-76 deg below the horizon), temp
    p10/median/p90 -73.0/-62.2/-47.8 C - the coldest land on the planet.

    LIGHT: the engine's own night (the sun is always far below the horizon) plus a PERMANENT aurora:
    the PerpetualAuroraExtension below makes WeatherSuite's MapComponent_PerpetualAurora keep a
    permanent RM_WS_DarkAurora condition on every map of this biome (glow, colour sweep speed and an
    off switch are Mod Settings in Weather Suite; numbers PROVISIONAL).

    PRECIPITATION, from the original concept sheet's phase ruling
    (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/worldgen_interactive_def.md:151-155,177-179, owner 2026-08-16):
    propane is liquid from -188 to -42 C, so across this whole band (-82..-42 C) it falls as RAIN and
    pools; ethane (liquid -183..-87) stays a gas here; water must never rain or snow on the nightside.
    So: RUT_PropaneRain, no snow at all. The rain carries rainRate 0 on purpose - it is not water, so
    it neither puts out fires, nor soaks pawns, nor waters plants. Where it pools: small patches of
    RM_PropaneShallow (FlowWorks' liquid-propane terrain; propane is the fuel the planet uses where
    other worlds use chemfuel). Weather weights and the pool threshold are PROVISIONAL first guesses.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_Umbra</defName>
    <label>Auroral Umbra</label>
    <description>The far end of the world, where the sun never rises: black ice that would be utterly dark if the sky ever rested. It never does. The strongest aurora on the planet burns overhead at every hour -- the magnetosphere slamming back together after its rude shock upstream -- sweeping green and violet across the ice, and it is the only light there is. It is cold enough here that propane falls as rain and gathers in clear, still pools that will burn the instant anything hot reaches them. The fast things run in blue flame, because nothing moves fluidly here without burning; the plants are crystal, and regrow overnight.</description>
    <workerClass>BiomeWorker_IceSheet</workerClass>  <!-- was AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_PropaneLakes; Alpha Biomes retired 2026-10-18. A worker scores tiles only at worldgen, which this frozen world never runs. -->

    <!-- OWNER RULING 2026-09-19 (RUT_UMBRA_ROADS_RULING_1): the ban STANDS. No
         roads in the Auroral Umbra, same as RUT_ExtremeDesert's "No roads through the deep
         dune". This flag was previously an unexamined default with no sheet behind
         it; it is now ruled and the sheet says so.
         MEASURED (2026-09-07 link export): 42 tiles carry stored road links,
         and 74 of their 78 links run internally - only 4 leave the region. So
         the ban costs almost no connectivity: it hides an internal web in the
         coldest land on the planet, not a route to anywhere.
         Nothing is destroyed by this. `potentialRoads` keeps every link in the
         world data (2,470 across the planet, unchanged); the flag only decides
         whether they DRAW. Flipping this to true restores all 42 tiles with no
         re-authoring, should the Assailant/Rakata-vault pilgrimage ever want a
         road in. -->
    <allowRoads>false</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.75</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/RUT_Umbra</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>110</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>RM_PackedSnow</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.87</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>RM_PackedIce</terrain>
        <min>0.87</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <!-- Where the propane rain gathers: small low pools of liquid propane (FlowWorks terrain; skipped
         without FlowWorks). Frequency/threshold PROVISIONAL - about 4% of the ground. -->
    <terrainPatchMakers>
      <li>
        <perlinFrequency>0.045</perlinFrequency>
        <thresholds>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.flowworks">
            <terrain>RM_PropaneShallow</terrain>
            <min>0.78</min>
            <max>999</max>
          </li>
        </thresholds>
      </li>
    </terrainPatchMakers>
    <!-- PROVISIONAL weights (AURORAL_UMBRA_RENAME_BACK_TO_DARK): propane rain about a third of the time,
         clear otherwise, dry lightning rare (ban 4: ignition needs a spark). No snow of any kind (owner
         2026-10-19: "it should NOT snow"); no water rain or fog (concept sheet: no water on the nightside). -->
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>60</Clear>
      <RUT_PropaneRain>30</RUT_PropaneRain>
      <DryThunderstorm>2</DryThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RUT_BurnerAscendant>0.03</RUT_BurnerAscendant>  <!-- the Burners, ascendant — apex of the Blue Desert's line (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, §4) -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RM_CrystalHorn>1.0</RM_CrystalHorn>  <!-- crystal horn -->
      <RM_FrostLeaf>0.6</RM_FrostLeaf>  <!-- frost leaf -->
      <!-- AB_RimeNodules 0.4 (rime nodules) removed 2026-10-18: Alpha Biomes retired; unguarded, it would be a cross-reference error. -->
      <!-- SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner review 2026-09-20: AB_CrystalFlower moved OUT
           (kept only at poison_forest, its "elsewhere") and PoisonShrub moved IN from
           wasteland (".8 cells, propane lakes"). Both rulings landed in
           rosters/the_propane_lakes.json and reached the game only through
           BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml's now-retired replace operation; transplanted here by
           BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1. -->
      <PoisonShrub MayRequire="Mlie.AdvancedBiomes">0.35</PoisonShrub>  <!-- poison shrub -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>1</wildPlantRegrowDays>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.WeatherSuite.PerpetualAuroraExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
